          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.52,
          "end": 10.03,
          "en": "which is the one with this input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.03,
          "end": 12.36,
          "en": "Now I mentioned all those lifecycle hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.36,
          "end": 15.06,
          "en": "and I mentioned that these would be methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.06,
          "end": 16.76,
          "en": "you can add to your Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.76,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "And with that, I don't mean methods you add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 22,
          "en": "in your methods option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22,
          "end": 24.32,
          "en": "Because in there, you really only add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.32,
          "end": 27.06,
          "en": "the methods you plan on calling yourself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.06,
          "end": 31.13,
          "en": "or which you want to call upon events, like clicks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.13,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "Instead, you add them right next to data and methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.84,
          "end": 37.97,
          "en": "Anywhere you want in this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.97,
          "end": 39.2,
          "en": "So for example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.2,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "towards the end of this app configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 47.87,
          "en": "Here, we could add the beforeCreate method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.87,
          "end": 50.65,
          "en": "which I showed on the slide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.65,
          "end": 53.03,
          "en": "You just add it as a method like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.03,
          "end": 55.763,
          "en": "and here we can console.log beforeCreate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.61,
          "end": 59.83,
          "en": "so that we get an idea for when this runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.83,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "And of course you could do more than just logging here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "You could send an HTTP request to a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 70.053,
          "en": "You could set a timer, you could do whatever you need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.01,
          "end": 73.653,
          "en": "If I now expand this again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.77,
          "end": 76.94,
          "en": "open the console and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.94,
          "end": 79.873,
          "en": "you see beforeCreate being logged here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 85.97,
          "en": "And actually, I'll comment out his log message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.97,
          "end": 89.43,
          "en": "at the very bottom so that we're not confused by that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.43,
          "end": 92.5,
          "en": "So let's go back to our Vue app again then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.5,
          "end": 94.797,
          "en": "reload, and we see beforeCreate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.95,
          "end": 100.95,
          "en": "If we do something else and go to the Sources tab here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 103.74000000000001,
          "en": "in the Chrome developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "we actually can also inspect our source code there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 109.59,
          "en": "And I'm showing this to you here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.59,
          "end": 112.6,
          "en": "because there's something neat we can do with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.6,
          "end": 115.66,
          "en": "We can actually find the beforeCreate method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.66,
          "end": 120.54,
          "en": "in the app.js file and click here to set a break point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.54,
          "end": 124.26,
          "en": "As a consequence, code execution will pause",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.26,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "when this is reached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 129.82,
          "en": "And if you now reload the page, you will see it pauses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.82,
          "end": 131.36,
          "en": "and you can always continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.36,
          "end": 133.41,
          "en": "by clicking the blue play button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.41,
          "end": 134.58,
          "en": "But the interesting thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.58,
          "end": 136.49,
          "en": "and the reason for why I'm doing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.49,
          "end": 139.27,
          "en": "is that you see there's nothing on the screen yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.27,
          "end": 140.54,
          "en": "As I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.54,
          "end": 144.07999999999998,
          "en": "in beforeCreate you won't see anything on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.07999999999998,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "At this point, actually not even the Vue app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 149.03300000000002,
          "en": "will have been fully initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.5,
          "end": 153.32,
          "en": "So let me click the blue button here to continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.32,
          "end": 156.143,
          "en": "and remove the break point by clicking on it again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.12,
          "end": 161.23,
          "en": "Let's now add the second hook, which is the created hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.23,
          "end": 163.197,
          "en": "At this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.197,
          "end": 166.46,
          "en": "the Vue app was initialized internally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.46,
          "end": 168.18,
          "en": "but it was not mounted yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.18,
          "end": 171.93,
          "en": "So visually, we'll still not see anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 176.93,
          "en": "If I reload, in the console we see created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.51,
          "end": 180.21,
          "en": "And if we go back to Sources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.21,
          "end": 184.07,
          "en": "and I add a break point in the created hook now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.07,
          "end": 186.5,
          "en": "if I reload, you see again at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.5,
          "end": 189.733,
          "en": "there's nothing on the screen, just as I explained.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.9,
          "end": 193.31,
          "en": "So let me remove the break point and continue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.31,
          "end": 196.02,
          "en": "and let's add more lifecycle hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 199.51,
          "en": "The next hook in place is beforeMount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.51,
          "end": 203.73,
          "en": "This triggers right before this app really is mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.73,
          "end": 207.03,
          "en": "So right before we see something on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.03,
          "end": 209.46,
          "en": "So we'll still not see anything here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.46,
          "end": 212.79,
          "en": "but we will see something in the next hook thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.79,
          "end": 213.993,
          "en": "which is mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.06,
          "end": 219.8,
          "en": "So here, let me console.log mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.8,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "And let's then save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 225.62,
          "en": "go back to the JavaScript console and reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.62,
          "end": 230.62,
          "en": "And we see beforeCreate, created, beforeMount and mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.73,
          "end": 236.2,
          "en": "But again, it's more interesting if we go to Sources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.2,
          "end": 241.2,
          "en": "and now add a break point in before mount and in mounted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.56,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "and now reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 246.62,
          "en": "And we first pause in beforeMount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.62,
          "end": 249.28,
          "en": "because that hook runs first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.28,
          "end": 251.323,
          "en": "And you see nothing on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.35,
          "end": 257.35,
          "en": "If you now click resume, so this blue play button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.38,
          "end": 260.57,
          "en": "we pause on the next break point, which is in mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.57,
          "end": 263.12,
          "en": "And now you see something on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.12,
          "end": 266.08,
          "en": "As I explained, because at this point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.08,
          "end": 269.2,
          "en": "this Vue app was mounted to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.2,
          "end": 273.02,
          "en": "It was initialized internally, all the data was processed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.02,
          "end": 274.79,
          "en": "the template was compiled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.79,
          "end": 277.623,
          "en": "and it's showing its output on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.36,
          "end": 282,
          "en": "So, with that, we can also remove those break points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282,
          "end": 283.233,
          "en": "and resume again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.18,
          "end": 289.33,
          "en": "Now with that, the creation life cycle here is finished,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.33,
          "end": 292.05,
          "en": "but I mentioned that we would have data changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.05,
          "end": 294.853,
          "en": "which also triggered their own lifecycle hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.13,
          "end": 299.57,
          "en": "So let's see those in action as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.57,
          "end": 301.83,
          "en": "After mounted here, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.83,
          "end": 304.97,
          "en": "as mentioned before, the exact position does not matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.97,
          "end": 307.533,
          "en": "but after Mount that I'll add beforeUpdate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 314.56,
          "en": "and console.log beforeUpdate here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 314.56,
          "end": 317.623,
          "en": "And I will also add updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 319.07,
          "end": 322.51,
          "en": "The difference will be that in beforeUpdate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.51,
          "end": 325.13,
          "en": "we'll not see the changes on the screen yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.13,
          "end": 326.963,
          "en": "In updated, we will.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.85,
          "end": 330.73,
          "en": "So if you go to the JavaScript console in the DevTools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330.73,
          "end": 334.75,
          "en": "and reload, we don't see those hooks being executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 334.75,
          "end": 337.13,
          "en": "because nothing was updated in this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 337.13,
          "end": 340.55,
          "en": "It was created, but nothing was updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 340.55,
          "end": 343.51,
          "en": "So now let's enter a new text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 343.51,
          "end": 345.95,
          "en": "And if I click Set Text now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 345.95,
          "end": 348.383,
          "en": "you see beforeUpdate and updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 349.35,
          "end": 351.67,
          "en": "And if you go to the Source tab again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 351.67,
          "end": 356.67,
          "en": "and add some break points in beforeUpdate and in updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 356.72,
          "end": 359.90999999999997,
          "en": "we can also see that if I changed is again, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 359.90999999999997,
          "end": 363.91,
          "en": "to add more exclamation marks, we now pause.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 363.91,
          "end": 366.79,
          "en": "And we first pause in beforeUpdate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 366.79,
          "end": 370.09,
          "en": "And you notice that the text output here on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 370.09,
          "end": 372.15,
          "en": "is still the old one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 372.15,
          "end": 373.2,
          "en": "Because, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.2,
          "end": 376.91,
          "en": "in beforeUpdate the update was not fully processed yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.91,
          "end": 379.46,
          "en": "It's not visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 379.46,
          "end": 382.6,
          "en": "If I resume, we pause in updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.6,
          "end": 385.11,
          "en": "And indeed at this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 385.11,
          "end": 390.11,
          "en": "the output has been processed and is visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 391.66,
          "end": 394.51,
          "en": "So again, I'm removing those break points and resuming,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 394.51,
          "end": 397.713,
          "en": "and that hopefully shows the updating process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.24,
          "end": 403.55,
          "en": "Now, as mentioned before, we also can unmount a Vue app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 403.55,
          "end": 406.61,
          "en": "even though we haven't done this thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 406.61,
          "end": 410.97,
          "en": "We then trigger the beforeUnmount and the unmounted hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 410.97,
          "end": 412.83,
          "en": "And as also mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 412.83,
          "end": 416.823,
          "en": "this unmounting process will become more relevant later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 418.04,
          "end": 420.663,
          "en": "Nonetheless, let's see it in action now already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 422.21,
          "end": 424.33,
          "en": "And for that back in code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 424.33,
          "end": 428.76,
          "en": "I'm going to add deep beforeUnmount hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 428.76,
          "end": 430.273,
          "en": "and console.log beforeUnmount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 434.81,
          "end": 439.69,
          "en": "And I'm also going to add the unmounted hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 439.69,
          "end": 444.61,
          "en": "and hence console.log unmounted here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 444.61,
          "end": 447.62,
          "en": "so that both those hooks are implemented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 447.62,
          "end": 449.453,
          "en": "and we log a message for them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 450.56,
          "end": 453.53,
          "en": "But at the moment, this app will never get unmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 453.53,
          "end": 456.92,
          "en": "We have no way of killing or removing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 456.92,
          "end": 460.23,
          "en": "But just as we have an app mount method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 460.23,
          "end": 464.79,
          "en": "we also have a app unmount method to remove a Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 464.79,
          "end": 467.01,
          "en": "Now you will rarely call this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 467.01,
          "end": 468.84000000000003,
          "en": "in a real application though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 468.84000000000003,
          "end": 473.84000000000003,
          "en": "Instead, you will later see a way more realistic scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 473.93,
          "end": 475.72,
          "en": "of unmounting apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 475.72,
          "end": 478.97,
          "en": "But at the moment we're missing a key prerequisite for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 478.97,
          "end": 482.003,
          "en": "so we're going to work with that unmount method instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 482.89,
          "end": 485.21,
          "en": "We could set a timer here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 485.21,
          "end": 488.6,
          "en": "and set it to three seconds, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 488.6,
          "end": 493.6,
          "en": "and then have a function in which we call unmount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 494.26,
          "end": 498.34,
          "en": "So that three seconds after the app was created and mounted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 498.34,
          "end": 501.03,
          "en": "we destroy it, we unmount it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 501.03,
          "end": 502.72,
          "en": "And if we now save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 502.72,
          "end": 506.03,
          "en": "you will see that after three seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 506.03,
          "end": 507.88,
          "en": "the app has gone on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 507.88,
          "end": 509.83,
          "en": "and we see beforeUnmount and unmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 511.41,
          "end": 514.57,
          "en": "And of course, again, we could also go to the sources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 518.01,
          "end": 521.576,
          "en": "and simply add break points here in beforeUnmount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 521.576,
          "end": 523.08,
          "en": "and in unmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 523.08,
          "end": 527.48,
          "en": "And reload and see how this pauses after three seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 527.48,
          "end": 530.59,
          "en": "First in beforeUnmount, at which point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 530.59,
          "end": 531.95,
          "en": "we still see the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 531.95,
          "end": 534.673,
          "en": "So that's the last chance to work with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 535.51,
          "end": 539.063,
          "en": "But then if I resume, it's removed in unmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 540.93,
          "end": 545.93,
          "en": "And that is the Vue lifecycle with all its hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 546.06,
          "end": 550.01,
          "en": "In reality, you will only need a few of those hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 550.01,
          "end": 552.52,
          "en": "Nonetheless, of course, I wanted to show them to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 552.52,
          "end": 555.45,
          "en": "because this is the complete guide after all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 555.45,
          "end": 559.04,
          "en": "and not the I show you some things guide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 559.04,
          "end": 562.31,
          "en": "Nonetheless, we'll especially see hooks like created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 562.31,
          "end": 565.98,
          "en": "mounted or unmounted in action throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 565.98,
          "end": 567.53,
          "en": "as well as updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 567.53,
          "end": 571.49,
          "en": "And with that, we can also leave this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 571.49,
          "end": 575.18,
          "en": "We now have a solid understanding of the basic features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 575.18,
          "end": 577.31,
          "en": "and not just of how to use them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 577.31,
          "end": 579.84,
          "en": "but also how they work under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 579.84,
          "end": 582.9,
          "en": "And with that, you already made a huge step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 582.9,
          "end": 586.263,
          "en": "in the right direction to becoming a Vue developer.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
